{"title":"Intermediate value property","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real\">real</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> is said to have the <b>intermediate value property</b> on an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Interval\" title=\"Interval\">interval</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da2e551d2ca2155b8d8f4935d2e9757722c9bab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a, b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> if, for each value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1acc6639de4f1c620680bec4adf3e668f4db723f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b041c557e15a9393c58bfeedd30d3c93f5c7de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, there is some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a0743a607d097b2fdd01aed91cbcafad03dcde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\in (a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f99d7ffcd7076b88dd905845c4f1136adacf327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(c) = v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, a function with the intermediate value property takes all intermediate values between any two points.\n</p><p>The simplest, and most important, examples of functions with this property are the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Continuous_function\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Continuous function\">continuous functions</a>.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Intermediate_value_property&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018091544\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 25/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 322/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1055/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.323      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.323      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3288:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018091544 and revision id 233340. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}